Source: hwsv4l2
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Max Lapshin <max@flussonic.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-dkms
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/flussonic/avmatrix-v4l2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: hwsv4l2-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers-arm64
Description: V4L2 driver for AVMatrix HWS capture cards (DKMS source)
 Every input of an AVMatrix HWS PCIe card gets a multi-planar V4L2 capture
 node whose buffers carry the picture, the frame's audio and per-frame
 metadata, laid out like those of the SDI cards.
 .
 The module is built by DKMS for every installed kernel. The package keeps
 HwsCapture, the other driver of these cards, from autoloading, since
 whichever loads first owns them.

Package: hwsv4l2-dev
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: V4L2 driver for AVMatrix HWS capture cards (client header)
 The headers a program needs to read the buffers of the hwsv4l2 nodes:
 pixel formats, the layout of the audio plane and the per-frame metadata.
